2026-09-27T07:42:27.0265369Z Description:
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0265725Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0266027Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0266767Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0267720Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0267802Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0268079Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0268375Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0268658Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0269209Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0269469Z ================
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0269589Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0269754Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0270133Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0270354Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0270461Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0270732Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0270901Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0271037Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0271709Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0272090Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0272755Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0273283Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0273389Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0273807Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0274337Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0274614Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0274903Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0275305Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0275395Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0275574Z ========
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0275677Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0276953Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0278356Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0278567Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0279020Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0279803Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0280405Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0358220Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0359336Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0360560Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0360810Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0361244Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0361720Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0363350Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0365332Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0366412Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0367934Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:42:27.0368308Z 
